@nsobid-4F5C96E2D97F45AC288BC67613EBEF0A

# Xenoblade Chronicles 2 3.0.1 - Disable anti-aliasing

@flag print_values
@flag offset_shift 0x100

// Disables the game's anti-aliasing: FXAA in the final composite and the
// temporal AA (tmaa).
//
// Both are switches in the post-effect parameter file the renderer parses
// (sub_7100716E68): "AntiAliasing" and "tmaa", each "on" or "off".
// sub_71007A1204 copies them into the frame's render state (+0xFC and +0x111),
// and sub_71007A0774 resets the state with AntiAliasing on. When either is on,
// the frame ends in the AA composite (FXAA, sub_710079C930) or the temporal
// resolve (sub_71007F7274), and tmaa also drives the temporal history and
// jitter users.
//
// Every write of the two switches now stores off. The frame then takes the
// renderer's own no-AA final composite, the path the parameter file selects
// when both are set to off, so FXAA, the temporal resolve and its jitter all
// stop.

@enabled
007A098C 7FF20339   // STRB WZR,[X19,#0xFC]: reset leaves AntiAliasing off (was STRB W16 = on)
007A1278 7FF20339   // STRB WZR,[X19,#0xFC]: AntiAliasing off for render mode 1, which forces it on (was STRB W20)
007A12F4 7F460439   // STRB WZR,[X19,#0x111]: tmaa off (was STRB W8 = parameter file value)
007A12FC 7FF20339   // STRB WZR,[X19,#0xFC]: AntiAliasing off (was STRB W8 = parameter file value)
@stop

// Offsets reverse-engineered against Xenoblade Chronicles 2 3.0.1 (Monolith
// engine, NVN). The retail build is symbol-stripped; every site was located by
// structure and byte-verified against the IDB before being written.
//
// https://github.com/RAMDRAGONS/switch-patches
